    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1054">

                <pb facs="0662" n="1712" xml:id="pg1712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.918/8–1453</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret<lb/>eyes
                            only</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-08-18">August 18, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I believe this telegram is worth your reading.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1054-f1"/>
                    We are working out the immediate problem in connection with the thorium nitrate
                    shipments in accordance with your decision, although the necessary assurances
                    from India have not yet been forthcoming. It is the second part of the message
                    which seems particularly important. Allen is usually an accurate and objective
                    reporter and if he is right in this case, as I am inclined to think he is, it
                    may well be that we have gone past the point of diminishing returns in several
                    areas. I can’t forget that we made all sorts of diplomatic efforts to persuade
                    Burma not to reject our assistance but, having taken that action, she seems to
                    be just as well off and our relations, if anything, are better. Foster has not
                    seen this message but we talked about the general subject of “diminishing
                    returns” before he left, and have started a pretty thorough and careful study of
                    the matter which will be tied in with the final Solarium Plan<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1054-f2"/> and will be ready for consideration by the Council
                    sometime after you return.</p>
                <closer><signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">alter</hi>] B. S[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">mith</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1054-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1054-f1-content">
                <p>The telegram to which Under Secretary Smith was referring was New Delhi telegram
                    318, Aug. 14, 1953, <ref target="#d1053"><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1054-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1054-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation regarding the Solarium Plan, see <ref target="frus1952-54v02p1"
                        >volume <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
